    "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nKimi K3 ModelSlim checkpoints can use different quantization precisions for the Q and full-rank G projections. Merging Q/K/V/G into one projection then fails during model initialization because all shards of a fused layer must have the same precision.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- On NPU, use the existing ModelSlim `is_layer_skipped()` checks to select separate projections when Q and G have different precisions.\r\n- Reuse the existing split construction and forward paths, and skip the fused QKV/G weight mapping for those layers.\r\n- Keep the existing fused path for compatible checkpoints. This change is independent of KV-cache dtype and MLAProlog.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\n- Verified that this patch has the same stable patch ID as the QKV/G changes extracted from #46921.\r\n- Verified that reapplying the extracted patch to the remaining C8 changes restores the complete original Git tree.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nNot run for this standalone branch.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format the changed file.\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests.\r\n- [ ] Update documentation if needed.\r\n- [ ] Provide standalone NPU accuracy and speed benchmark results.\r\n- [x] Reuse the existing model construction, forward, and loading paths.\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41372382657](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41372382657)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41372382572](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41372382572)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41372382592](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41372382592)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n\r\n> [!TIP]\r\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\r\n>\r\n> ```text\r\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\r\n> ```\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
